---
description: Rules for recreating the jungle piranha lake map in Blender
alwaysApply: true
---

PROJECT GOAL

Recreate the supplied jungle concept as closely as possible from the main gameplay camera.

The arena is a raised square platform standing above a jungle lake containing stylized piranhas.

The target style is:
- polished stylized 3D;
- arcade party-game aesthetic;
- medium-poly rather than extreme low-poly;
- clean silhouettes;
- rounded bevels;
- large readable shapes;
- saturated tropical colors;
- soft lighting;
- no photorealism.

NON-DESTRUCTIVE RULES

- Never delete or rename gameplay objects.
- Never change gameplay collisions, origins or transforms without approval.
- Keep gameplay geometry separate from visual geometry.
- Place all new objects inside MAP_JUNGLE_UPGRADE.
- Save a new version before every major phase.
- Do not apply destructive modifiers until the result has been validated.
- Never generate the entire map in one operation.
- After each phase, create a viewport screenshot and a camera render.

REFERENCE RULES

- Treat the supplied concept image as the main visual reference.
- Match the concept from the MAIN_GAME_CAMERA.
- Preserve the platform proportions and gameplay area.
- Match large shapes before adding details.
- Prioritize silhouette, placement, scale and color over small decorations.
- Do not invent large elements that are absent from the reference.
- Hidden areas may be completed consistently with the visible design.

GEOMETRY QUALITY

Do not use extreme low-poly geometry.

Recommended quality:
- small props: 300–1500 triangles;
- plants: 500–3000 triangles;
- trees: 1500–6000 triangles;
- large rocks: 800–4000 triangles;
- hero objects: 3000–12000 triangles.

Use:
- bevel modifiers;
- weighted normals;
- shade smooth by angle;
- controlled polygon density;
- clean topology;
- modular assets;
- linked instances.

Avoid:
- primitive cubes without shaping;
- perfectly sharp edges;
- noisy subdivision;
- excessive micro-details;
- photorealistic scanned assets.

PLACEMENT RULES

- Objects must not intersect each other visibly.
- Tree trunks must reach the terrain.
- Rocks must sit partly inside the ground, not float above it.
- Plants must follow terrain normals.
- Vines must connect to actual support points.
- Waterfalls must start at a source and terminate in a lower body of water.
- Water must follow a logical elevation hierarchy.
- No object may intersect the arena or block gameplay visibility.
- Keep the center of the gameplay platform readable.

VALIDATION

After every placement phase:
- detect mesh intersections;
- detect floating objects;
- detect objects below the terrain;
- detect duplicated objects;
- detect missing materials;
- detect unapplied negative scale;
- detect incorrect normals;
- verify collection membership;
- render from MAIN_GAME_CAMERA.